ace of saying  that jimmy needed help which to his  credit is true but he came at kim in the  worst way and totally turned her against  him in the process he told her what was  going on in a way that assumed that she  couldn't see that jimmy was having  problems and since in his mind no one  would make the decision to leave her job  he insisted that jimmy must have  influenced her decision in some way she  ended up unloading on him saying do you  have any idea how insulting that is i  make my own decisions for my own reasons  he throws more fuel on the fire saying  you know who really knew jimmy chuck and  she decides that it wouldn't be a big  deal to go after him picking up where  jimmy had already started she assures  her husband that she's prepared to go  through with it and while he doesn't  look nearly as certain you can imagine  that he'll get on board with whatever it  is she wants to do when this series  started it almost functioned as two  shows in one you have what was going on  with jimmy and then you had mike's story  that went off in its own direction as we  near the end things have been drawn  together with the introduction of lalo  mike's story is somewhat overshadowed by  that and what's happening with nacho we  know how things end for mike and at this  point we can see how he got on the  slippery slope of being one of gus's  most trusted guys he took the job  helping with the super lab thinking that  there was a low chance of any violence  being involved and ended up having to  kill someone he had become friends with  in verner that put him on a  self-destructive path in the beginning  of season 5 until gus intervened and  sent him off to mexico there he  explained to him that he needed a  soldier and i'm not sure if he made  enough of a case to have mike set aside  his personal code the thing that had  kept him from going all in on working  with him in the first place but it  certainly opened up the path in season 5  it felt like mike made a decision to  play the hand he was dealt in other  words do what he's good at in service of  providing for kaylee after he's gone  which is pretty rough when you think  about how it all plays out now that gus  has failed to take out lalo it seems  like their showdown will take over most  of the action on that side of the story  and i think i should leave things there  i'm super excited to find out what  happens with gene why kim doesn't appear  to be around anymore during the breaking  bad timeline how this whole thing plays  out with howard whether or not nacho and  his dad make it out and then what  happens to lalo so let me know in the  comments what you're most interested in  what you're thinking about let me know  if you have any questions about what  happened in the series so far tell me  how you think it might end and what you  most want to see happen in this final  season we're coming to the end of the  breaking bad universe and i can't wait  to see how it all ends please like this  video if you enjoyed it please subscribe  to my channel if you haven't already  i'll be doing episode recaps and weekly  bonus videos all throughout this season  so make sure you come back and thanks  for watching i'll talk to you soon


